termbox2.h is upstream termbox2 (MIT licensed) with the patches in patches/
applied:

  https://github.com/termbox/termbox2
  commit cdf62e9990d8b200768780080fb10a4e2f680051 (2026-09-03, version 2.7.0-dev)
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/termbox/termbox2/cdf62e9990d8b200768780080fb10a4e2f680051/termbox2.h

  patches/0001-platform-layer.patch
      Moves the operating system calls of tb_init_file, tb_init_rwfd,
      tb_deinit, wait_event, bytebuf_flush and tb_strerror into static
      functions at the end of the implementation (open_tty, init_fds,
      wait_input, write_output, now_ms, ...); init_term_attrs,
      init_resize_handler and update_term_size stay where they are.
      Pure refactoring on POSIX systems.

  patches/0002-windows-console.patch
      Adds a Windows definition of each of those functions: the Windows
      console in virtual terminal mode, read through ReadConsoleInputW.

Each patch file starts with a description of what it does and why. The
compile-time options Term::Fabulous builds the header with live in
tf_termbox.h; termbox2.c is the one translation unit that defines TB_IMPL.

Updating termbox2
-----------------

1. Download the new upstream termbox2.h over src/termbox2.h.
2. Apply the patches in order from src/:

       patch termbox2.h patches/0001-platform-layer.patch
       patch termbox2.h patches/0002-windows-console.patch

   When a hunk no longer applies, port it by hand: upstream may have
   moved a system call into or out of the functions the platform layer
   replaces (tb_init_file, tb_init_rwfd, init_term_attrs,
   init_resize_handler, update_term_size, tb_deinit, wait_event,
   bytebuf_flush, tb_strerror, tb_set_input_mode, load_terminfo and
   load_builtin_caps). Then regenerate the patches: 0001 is the
   difference between upstream and the header without its _WIN32 parts,
   0002 the rest.
3. Rebuild and run t/termbox.t and t/terminal-termbox.t here, then
   build and test on Windows (see the WINDOWS section of
   lib/Term/Fabulous/Termbox.pm). The checks below apply as well.

The Term::Fabulous input parser in termbox2.c (Alt keys, SGR mouse
reports, kitty keyboard protocol key reports) hooks in through
tb_set_func(TB_FUNC_EXTRACT_PRE) and reads the input buffer global.in
directly. Upstream marks tb_set_func and TB_FUNC_EXTRACT_PRE for removal
in version 3.x (ABI version 3, see the "Deprecation notice" in
termbox2.h). Before taking a 3.x release, port tf_install_input_parser()
to its replacement, then run t/termbox.t: it feeds raw escape sequences
through the parser.

Inline mode (tf_init_inline_rwfd() in termbox2.c) repeats the steps of
tb_init_rwfd() with termbox2's static init functions and empties the
TB_CAP_ENTER_CA, TB_CAP_EXIT_CA and TB_CAP_CLEAR_SCREEN entries of
global.caps. The terminal queries (tf_cursor_position(),
tf_kitty_keyboard_query(), tf_sixel_query()) wait with wait_input() of
the platform layer, with a NULL resized argument so that a resize stays
pending for tb_peek_event, and append to global.in; tf_cells_differ()
and tf_invalidate_cells() read and write the cells of global.back and
global.front through termbox2's static cellbuf_get(), cell_cmp() and
cell_set() (tf_invalidate_cells() marks a cell the way tb_present()
marks the hidden cells of a wide glyph), and tf_reset_attrs() resets
global.last_fg and global.last_bg. tf_input_ended() and
tf_window_cell_size() ask the operating system questions termbox2 never
asks (FIONREAD, TIOCGWINSZ) and have POSIX and Windows versions of their
own. After updating termbox2.h, compare tb_init_rwfd() with
tf_init_inline_rwfd() and check that tb_deinit() and resize_cellbufs()
still take the screen only through those capabilities; the "inline
mode" subtest of t/termbox.t checks the output.
